# Halisi Events — Event Discovery & Ticketing

A browser-based event listing and ticket registration site. Users can browse events happening in Nairobi, search/filter them, see how far each one is from their current location, register for a pass via M-Pesa, and view/scan their ticket as a QR code.

## Features

- **Event browsing** — events are rendered dynamically from a JavaScript data array (`eventsData`), each with a title, date, venue, category, price, and image.
- **Search** — a live search bar filters events by title, venue, or category as the user types.
- **Location-based sorting ("near you")** — using the browser's Geolocation API, events are sorted nearest-first once the user grants location access, with the distance (in km) shown on each card. If location access is denied or unavailable, the app falls back gracefully to showing events unsorted.
- **Registration popup** — clicking "Get Pass" opens an in-page modal collecting the user's name, email, and M-Pesa phone number, without navigating away from the events page.
- **Ticket generation** — on submission, a unique ticket ID is generated and saved to the browser's `localStorage`, then the user is redirected to a QR code ticket page.
- **QR code ticket page** — displays the registered event, holder name, ticket ID, and a scannable QR code generated from the ticket data.
- **Gate scanning simulation** — a "Scan" button marks the ticket as used and blocks re-entry on a second scan; a "Delete" button clears the active ticket.
- **Data persistence** — ticket data persists across page loads/navigation using `localStorage`, so the ticket remains available if the browser is closed and reopened.

## Tech Used

- HTML5 (semantic structure: header, nav, main, section, footer)
- CSS3 (custom properties, responsive design with mobile/tablet/desktop breakpoints, hover/transition animations)
- Vanilla JavaScript (DOM manipulation, event handling, Geolocation API, localStorage)
- [QRCode.js](https://github.com/davidshimjs/qrcodejs) for QR code generation
- Font Awesome for icons

## How to Run

Geolocation requires a secure context (`https://` or `localhost`) — opening the HTML file directly (`file://`) will silently block the location prompt. To run locally:

1. Open this project folder in VS Code.
2. Install the **Live Server** extension.
3. Right-click `Halisi-events.html` → **Open with Live Server**.
4. Allow location access when prompted, to see events sorted by distance.

## Project Structure

```
├── Halisi-events.html   # Browse/search events, registration popup
├── qrcode.html           # Ticket display + QR code + gate scanner
├── script.js              # All application logic
├── styles.css             # Base styles
├── skiddle-theme.css      # Visual theme layer (loaded after styles.css)
└── README.md
```

## Known Issues / Limitations

- Venue coordinates in `eventsData` are approximate landmark estimates and should be verified precisely (e.g. via Google Maps) for fully accurate distance calculations.
- M-Pesa payment is captured as a phone number field only — no live payment/STK push integration is connected; this is a front-end simulation of the registration flow.
